<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Buying vs Renting</span>
<h1>Teachers: Rent vs Buy Decision for Hanoi Motorbikes</h1>
<p>Every teacher who lands a contract in Hanoi faces the same first-week question behind the housing search and the SIM card: buy a motorbike or rent one for the length of the posting? This guide grades the decision honestly, the way a good rubric grades anything, with criteria stated in advance, no numbers invented, and every live fact sent to the official sources that actually own it. The rental rates quoted here can be verified today at one counter in Long Bien; the purchase prices deliberately are not quoted at all, because the market owns those numbers and changes them without consulting writers.</p>
<p>The machines, the briefing and the honest numbers come from Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu, 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, Hanoi, open daily 09:00 to 21:00, where the desk has advised enough teachers to know the decision arrives with the contract and leaves with the removal truck. Begin at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-for-sale/">motorbike for sale hub</a>, study the long-stay arrangements on the <a href="/monthly-motorbike-rental-hanoi/">monthly motorbike rental</a> page, check the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">Hanoi motorbike rental cost</a> hub, review the <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a> for maintenance and safety, and keep <a href="/renting-a-motorbike-in-vietnam/">renting a motorbike in Vietnam</a> open for the legal layer.</p>
